<h1>OpenZiti for OpenWRT</h1>

<p>Signed <code>opkg</code> feed for <a href="https://openziti.io">OpenZiti</a> on OpenWRT 23.05+ routers.</p>

<p>Source: <a href="https://github.com/openziti/ziti-openwrt">github.com/openziti/ziti-openwrt</a> &middot;
   <a href="https://github.com/openziti/ziti-openwrt/blob/main/docs/installing.md">install guide</a> &middot;
   <a href="https://github.com/openziti/ziti-openwrt/blob/main/docs/compatibility.md">compatibility</a></p>

<h2>What's in the feed</h2>

<ul>
  <li><code>ziti-edge-tunnel</code> &mdash; the C tunneler</li>
  <li><code>ziti-router</code> &mdash; the Go edge router (statically linked)</li>
  <li><code>luci-app-ziti</code> &mdash; LuCI web UI</li>
  <li><code>llhttp9</code> &mdash; runtime dep for the tunneler</li>
</ul>

<h2>Per-architecture feed URLs</h2>

<p>Pick the URL that matches what your device reports from <code>opkg print-architecture</code>.</p>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Arch</th>
    <th>Devices</th>
    <th>Feed</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>aarch64_cortex-a53_neon-vfpv4</code></td>
    <td>GL.iNet QSDK (GL-BE3600, GL-MT6000, GL-AXT1800, ...)</td>
    <td><a href="aarch64_cortex-a53_neon-vfpv4/">aarch64_cortex-a53_neon-vfpv4/</a></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>aarch64_cortex-a53</code></td>
    <td>mvebu Cortex-A53 (NanoPi R2S, FriendlyELEC NEO3, ESPRESSObin, ...)</td>
    <td><a href="aarch64_cortex-a53/">aarch64_cortex-a53/</a></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>x86_64</code></td>
    <td>OpenWRT x86_64 routers and VMs</td>
    <td><a href="x86_64/">x86_64/</a></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>Install on the device</h2>

<pre><code># 1. Trust the feed's signing key
mkdir -p /etc/opkg/keys
curl -fsSL @@BASE_URL@@/pub.key -o /tmp/pub.key
KEYID=$(usign -F -p /tmp/pub.key)
mv /tmp/pub.key /etc/opkg/keys/$KEYID

# 2. Add the feed (substitute &lt;arch&gt; with one of the dirs above)
echo "src/gz openziti @@BASE_URL@@/&lt;arch&gt;" &gt;&gt; /etc/opkg/customfeeds.conf

# 3. Install
opkg update
opkg install ziti-edge-tunnel luci-app-ziti ziti-router</code></pre>

<p>For GL.iNet QSDK firmware (GL-BE3600 et al), use <code>aarch64_cortex-a53_neon-vfpv4</code>. The arch label is repacked server-side; no client-side repack needed. Details: <a href="https://github.com/openziti/ziti-openwrt/blob/main/docs/install-gl-inet.md">install-gl-inet.md</a>.</p>

<h2>Public key</h2>

<p>The feed is signed with usign. Direct link: <a href="pub.key">pub.key</a>. Compute its fingerprint with <code>usign -F -p pub.key</code> and install on the device at <code>/etc/opkg/keys/&lt;fingerprint&gt;</code>.</p>

